From 50f3cfa18855a87f5c8da9e6cfde9a95515618b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:00:27 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 29/30] apps: Adds wlmcalclock, a calendar clock DockApp.

Shows the time on a LED-style display, and weekday, day of the month
and month on a calendar page below; similar to Window Maker's `wmclock`.

Weekday and month are the abbreviated names of the session's locale
(LC_TIME, via nl_langinfo), in upper case as per LC_CTYPE, eg. "MON 26
OCT" in English, or "SEG 26 OUT" in Brazilian Portuguese. Other locale
categories remain "C".

Options: --twelve_hour shows the time in 12-hour format, with an AM/PM
indicator; --seconds also shows seconds.

The app wakes up only on each full minute (or second, with --seconds).
The time to show is taken from the timers' clock (gettimeofday): time()
may be served from a coarse clock that still shows the previous second
when the timer fires, and the display then missed the new minute.

Formatting and the computation of the next wakeup are in wlm_calendar,
with unit tests run as `apps_test`. Adds a .desktop file and an icon.

Signed-off-by: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
